  "renderer_only": [
    "Text gate: the live ETL publishes a note, region note or MediaRef attribute value only from an io-approved per-object allowlist. The renderer publishes what the store view holds and withholds any text that default_text_gate flags (the R-18 detector or the live ETL's scanner). An io-visible decision. In P(fixture) only N0010 trips it (no_delta_cases.withheld_by_text_gate).",
    "The same gate also covers Event.description, Media.desc (the media title falls back to the Gramps ID), the path and desc of a place URL (a contact URL or an e-mail type is dropped), citation titles and the value of a note LINK tag (userinfo in an href is refused). The live ETL publishes all of these as written. No case in P(fixture) trips them; test_render_rules.OtherFreeTextIsGated covers each."
  ],
  "rules": {
    "excluded-place": {
      "reference": "BRD2 section 11.1 (5.3), sync.md 5.3, D2-32, Q2-02 item 2",
      "summary": "The renderer never publishes a street-level or home-like place (Street, Building, Number, Farm, or a custom type matching house|home|residence|address|apartment|apt|lot|farm). Its place file is not written, it leaves place/index.json, and every event or place reference to it is re-pointed to the nearest kept ancestor. The live ETL publishes all of them."
    }
  },
  "version": 1
}
